  "query_preview": "..Isolated showers and thunderstorms have tapered off\nearly this morning over the Navajo nation with minimal heavy rain\nimpacts seen there. For this weekend a strong ridge will continue\nto build across the Four Corners before slightly wobbling \neastward. Even with a slight shift in the general placement of \nthis pressure system, above normal afternoon high temperatures and\ndaily thunderstorm chances will remain through the entire \nforecast period. We are also expecting an influx of additional \nmoisture from the southeast starting Sunday and lasting through \nthe first half of next week at least. An Extreme Heat Warning \nremains in effect for elevations below 4000' at the Grand Canyon \nand for Marble/Glen Canyons through Sunday evening. Given a major\nheat risk and highs near 110 for the low elevations of Yavapai \ncounty, the Extreme Heat Warning for today was expanded there. \nAlthough these are the only areas where we have a heat product in \neffect, all lower elevation locations will be experiencing hot \ndaytime highs through the next several days, so avoid strenuous \nactivity during the middle of the day and stay hydrated! As for \nprecipitation, greatest chances will be across the higher terrain \neach afternoon/early evening. Flash flooding will likely be the \nmain concern with all the recent rainfall across much of our area.",
